course: dictionary
lesson: 8023
title: Shiny things that send light back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A reflector is something with a shiny surface that sends light back to where it came from. Context helps you find its meaning. «Drivers must be able to see you, so at night a bike has a white light at the front, a red light at the back and reflectors.» The words «so drivers can see you» tell you why reflectors are there.
explain: «Reflectors are made of tiny corner shapes that send light straight back to where it came from, such as a driver's headlights.» Read the clue «send light straight back» and then test it. If a reflector sends light back, a driver's headlights shine on the bike and the reflector glows back at the driver.
explain: Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. «At night a bike needs a white light at the front, a red light at the back and reflectors, so drivers can see it.» Put in "shiny thing that sends light back" and it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A reflector is something with a shiny surface that sends light back towards where it came from.
fact: «Reflector strips» and «reflector vests» help drivers see people at night.
fact: Cat's eyes, the little reflectors set into the middle of the road, were invented by Percy Shaw in England in 1934.
fact: Light bounces off shiny surfaces, so telescopes and torches also use reflectors.
exercise: What is a reflector? | *Something shiny that sends light back to where it came from | A tiny light that flashes on a bike | Something that makes a loud noise | A kind of road sign with words
exercise: «At night a bike needs a white light at the front, a red light at the back and reflectors, so drivers can see it.» Why does a bike have reflectors? | *So drivers can see it | To grow taller | To make the bike go faster | To keep the rider warm
exercise: «Reflectors are made of tiny corner shapes that send light straight back.» Find and copy one word that means give out again. | *send | shapes | corner | tiny
test: «Cat's eyes, the little reflectors set into the middle of the road, were invented by Percy Shaw in England in 1934.» Where were cat's eyes invented? | Scotland | Germany | Australia | *England
test: A cyclist puts reflectors on her school bag. Why? | To look fashionable | To keep rain out | *So drivers can see the bag at night | To make the bag heavier
exam: Which of these uses reflectors besides bikes? | *A torch | Shoes | A kettle | A sandwich
